## Rollback procedure

1. Revert the last merge on `main` or roll back the GitOps promotion PR.
2. Confirm the previous container image tag is live in the cluster.
3. Run smoke tests against {% if layout == 'grpc' %}gRPC `HealthService.Check`{% else %}`/healthz` on port {{ port }}{% endif %}.

{% elif layout == 'worker' -%}
## Rollback procedure

1. Scale the deployment to zero or pause the consumer subscription.
2. Roll back the image tag and replay dead-letter messages after validation.
3. Confirm queue depth and error rate return to baseline.

## Graceful drain

- Send `SIGTERM` and allow in-flight messages to finish before the pod is killed.
- Set `terminationGracePeriodSeconds` high enough for your longest handler.

{% elif layout == 'scheduled-job' -%}
## Rollback procedure

1. Suspend the Kubernetes `CronJob` if the latest run misbehaved.
2. Roll back the container image on the CronJob template.
3. Inspect the last successful job logs before re-enabling the schedule.

## Missed-run alert

- Alert when no successful job completion occurs within `2 * schedule_interval`.
- Document the schedule and SLO in your observability repo.

